  "id": "Compound::DB00792 - Gene::3269",
  "verbalization": "Tripelennamine is closely related to several compounds that share a common structural feature of being histamine-1 receptor antagonists, as indicated by their shared lowest common ancestors. This suggests that Tripelennamine may also exhibit similar properties, potentially acting as a histamine-1 receptor antagonist. The evidence points to a possible mechanism where Tripelennamine, through structural similarity to other compounds like Captodiame and Pheniramine, binds to Hrh1, a protein involved in histamine signaling. The recurring theme of histamine-1 receptor antagonism across the related compounds implies a potential functional link between Tripelennamine and Hrh1, possibly through a shared mechanism of action. The integration of structural and functional similarities, along with the presence of a common ancestor in the histamine-1 receptor antagonist class, supports the hypothesis that Tripelennamine may interact with Hrh1 in a manner consistent with its structural relatives.",
